abstract: "Portable zero-dependency C11 whole-organism simulation engine (6,776 B/world) with 8 portable IEEE-754 deterministic math functions yielding 0-bit identical SHA-256 receipts across Win64 Clang and Linux GCC, an 11-slot int64 integer energy ledger, 18 structural circuit ablations, XPBD soft-body hydrostat, packed b1.58 ganglia, a software read-only WSE-12 self-editing guard, and an 825-check & 100-milestone Clean-Slate v3.0 test harness, paired with 68 Lean 4.35.0 theorems (6-kernel Palomar contract) covering unbounded-Int 10-field (Ledger10) and 11-slot (Ledger11) models, helper encodings, and 8 adversarial refutations (AdversarialTests.lean), plus 18 explicitly labeled closed numeral identities and 4 exported receipt constant checks. The C11 engine is tested, not formally proved. AI-assisted independent research under human direction; not peer-reviewed; cognitive indicators are strictly computational proxies."
